## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses practical data ingestion resilience, including handling mixed encodings and multi-channel sources (SFTP for CSVs, REST for JSON), along with end-to-end lineage and data quality understanding.

## Key Concepts
- Encoding detection and transcoding at ingestion
- Incremental loading using per-file watermarks
- Mapping Data Flows for Parquet conversion and star schema population in Azure Synapse
- Data quality and schema validation checks
- Purview lineage integration for traceability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Azure Function to detect encoding and transcode to UTF-8
const fs = require('fs');
module.exports = async function (context, myBlob) {
    const buffer = Buffer.from(myBlob);
    const isUtf16 = buffer[0] === 0xFF && buffer[1] === 0xFE;
    let content;

    if (isUtf16) {
        content = buffer.toString('utf16le');
    } else {
        content = buffer.toString('utf8');
    }

    context.bindings.outputBlob = content;
};
```

